-- title:
--   Proposition 3.1 — explicit maximal order and dyadic splitting
-- statement:
--   For $F=\mathbb Q(\sqrt{17})$, $D=(-1,-3)_F$, and $O=O_F\langle1,i,u,v\rangle$, the lattice $O$ is a maximal order with unit reduced discriminant. At every finite prime $R$, $D_R$ is split. At $Q=(2,\omega)$ the specified matrices extend to a splitting with
--   $$\psi:D_Q\simeq M_2(\mathbb Q_2),\qquad\psi(O_Q)=M_2(\mathbb Z_2).$$
--   Under it, reduced norm and trace become matrix determinant and trace. The even-root equations for $\alpha,z$ and the existence of the distinguished finite place are asserted as conclusions. This supplies the arithmetic representation used at every graph level.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the fixed arithmetic objects and labeled graphs → the shared concrete definitions over the quadratic algebra, ZMod residues, and zero-based Fin label indices; reason: the representations preserve the field, orders, incidences, and all source instances
--   - encoding: unit reduced discriminant → unit ideal generated by trace-pairing determinants; reason: for an order the trace discriminant is the square of the reduced discriminant, so unit ideals are equivalent
--   - encoding: the completion identified with Q2 at Q → a ring isomorphism agreeing with the explicit global splitting, with norm and trace expressed through its scalar embedding; reason: this avoids assuming a completion identification as a hypothesis
-- source:
--   Olga Kharlampovich, Igor Pak, Alina Vdovina, STOC 2027 submission #136 (October 2026), source.pdf SHA-256 27d691a82d8af863e511e7e6b00cee95779d914645846d2974f876836db8f83b, p.11 (PDF p.12), Proposition 3.1. https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/136.pdf

import Definitions.Def_RamanujanLiftTower136_Tower_Ideals

namespace RamanujanLiftTower136.Tower

theorem explicit_maximal_order :
  maximalOrder (orderLattice : Set D) ∧ unitDiscriminant (orderLattice : Set D) ∧
  (∀ R : Place, Nonempty (LocalD R ≃ₐ[LocalField R] Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) (LocalField R))) ∧
  (alpha^2 + 3*alpha - 2 = 0 ∧ alpha ∈ Ideal.span {(2 : ℤ_[2])}) ∧
  (zeta^2 + zeta + 2 = 0 ∧ zeta ∈ Ideal.span {(2 : ℤ_[2])}) ∧
  (∃ R : Place, R.asIdeal = Q) ∧
  ∀ R : Place, R.asIdeal = Q →
    ∃ e : LocalD R ≃+* Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℚ_[2],
      (∀ x, e (localize R x) = psi x) ∧
      (∀ x, localSplitting R x = e x) ∧
      e '' completed (orderLattice : Set D) R = {a | ∀ i j, ‖a i j‖ ≤ 1} ∧
      (∀ x, Matrix.det (e x) = (e (algebraMap (LocalField R) (LocalD R) (localNrd R x))) 0 0) ∧
      (∀ x, Matrix.trace (e x) = (e (algebraMap (LocalField R) (LocalD R) (localTrd R x))) 0 0) := by sorry

end RamanujanLiftTower136.Tower
